   "evidence": "grep `\u27e8map .*continuous_map|\u27e8BasedMap.map` finds the anonymous constructor at Based.lean:96-97, Retract.lean:122,126,148 and DoubleLoop.lean:106. Based.lean declares only `def map` (line 61) and `theorem continuous_map` (line 85), with no named continuous version.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Topology/MappingSpace/Based.lean",
   "fix": "Add a named continuous version `BasedMap.mapContinuousMap g hg : C(BasedMap B X b\u2080 x, BasedMap B Y b\u2080 y)` in Based.lean, with a `@[simp]` `_apply` lemma and `_id`/`_comp` lemmas, and state the four theorems in terms of it.",
   "issue": "`BasedMap.map` exists only as a plain function. The new public statements build its continuous version by hand as `\u27e8map g hg, continuous_map g hg\u27e9`: `homotopic_map_of_homotopicRel` (Based.lean:96-97), `BasedMap.injective_singularHomologyMap_map_of_homotopicRel` (Retract.lean:122), `BasedMap.injective_singularHomologyMap_map_of_surjective_singularHomologyMap` (Retract.lean:148), `IsFramedTube.injective_singularHomologyMap_inclEvalPreimage_comp_map` (DoubleLoop.lean:106), plus the proof term at Retract.lean:126. Users must rebuild this exact term to match the statements, and there are no id/comp lemmas for it, which is why Retract.lean:127-131 needs `convert` with `ext` and `map_comp`/`map_id`.",
   "line": 93
  }
 ],
